{"skill":{"slug":"notion","displayName":"Notion"},"version":{"version":"1.0.0","createdAt":1767545360889,"changelog":"","changelogSource":null,"license":null,"files":[{"path":"SKILL.md","size":5039,"sha256":"1002bcb8230ff496b65c2cb030737ed561c8c85fa1f823bed9192550e282a6fa","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":1792,"sha256":"8804aaa39cbb5fdf56daa9d64cf15f38952fc8e3315d63725a66daa1746818d8","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"clean","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789013586088,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"f5af8c9f858de5b4a90647a164aa89c0b5db270da55910914cb573a6bc768c1a","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/f5af8c9f858de5b4a90647a164aa89c0b5db270da55910914cb573a6bc768c1a","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","analysis":"Type: OpenClaw Skill\nName: notion\nVersion: 1.0.0\n\nThe skill is designed to interact with the Notion API. It instructs the user to store their Notion API key locally in `~/.config/notion/api_key` and then uses `cat` to read this key for authentication with `curl` commands. All network requests are directed to the legitimate Notion API endpoint (`https://api.notion.com`). There is no evidence of data exfiltration to unauthorized endpoints, malicious execution, persistence mechanisms, or prompt injection attempts aimed at subverting the agent for harmful purposes. The file access and network calls are directly aligned with the stated purpose of providing Notion API functionality.","source":"palm","checkedAt":1779159618327},"skillspector":{"status":"clean","normalizedStatus":"clean","score":8,"severity":"LOW","recommendation":"SAFE","issueCount":2,"checkedAt":1789013586088},"llm":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","confidence":"high","summary":"This is a straightforward Notion API helper skill, but users should protect the Notion token and be careful with commands that create or update workspace content.","dimensions":[{"detail":"The skill uses a local Notion API token and sends requests to api.notion.com, which is proportionate for a Notion integration, but the setup stores the token in a plaintext file without explicit permission-hardening guidance.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"note"},{"detail":"There is no installer, executable script, dependency, remote payload retrieval, or automatic setup beyond user-run shell snippets.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"Read and write operations are labeled by action, but the skill does not add a prominent warning that POST and PATCH examples modify live Notion workspace content.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The only local persistence is the Notion API key file under ~/.config/notion; Notion-side changes are user-directed through explicit create/update examples and are not hidden or automatic.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The stated purpose is to create, read, and update Notion pages, data sources, and blocks, and the documented curl examples match that purpose.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"ok"}],"guidance":"Before installing, treat the Notion API key as a secret: store it with owner-only permissions, avoid exposing it in logs or screenshots, and grant the Notion integration access only to pages or data sources it needs. Run POST and PATCH examples only when you intend to create or change live Notion content, preferably testing on non-production pages first.","findings":"[SQP-2] expected: The plaintext Notion token setup is a real hardening gap, but using a Notion token is necessary for the skill's stated API purpose and there is no evidence of hidden credential collection or exfiltration.\n[SQP-2] expected: The create, update, and append examples perform persistent Notion changes, but those operations are directly aligned with the skill description and are visibly labeled rather than concealed.\n[T09] expected: The file-permission concern is valid user guidance for the documented ~/.config/notion/api_key storage, but it does not make the package suspicious because no automatic installer or privilege escalation is present.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789013586088}}}}}